<title>MEXICO: MEXICO REVISED JUNE TRADE SURPLUS WIDENS.</title>
<headline>MEXICO REVISED JUNE TRADE SURPLUS WIDENS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's revised trade balance surplus for June was $308 million, the Finance Ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Exports in June were $9.421 billion, while imports were $9.113 billion, it said.</p>
<p>The preliminary trade balance for June was originally reported as a surplus of $182 million.  </p>
<p>		    June 97  PCT DIFF   JAN-June 97  YR AGO/</p>
<p>								    PCT DIFF</p>
<p>TRADE SURPLUS	  O.308     n/a	 2.091	    n/a</p>
<p>  EXPORTS		9.421   +23.7 pct  52.420	+15.3 pct</p>
<p>   Petroleum -	 0.854   -13.3 pct   5.647	+ 5.4 pct</p>
<p>   Manufacturing -   8.268   +30.0 pct  44.127	+17.4 pct</p>
<p>   Agriculture -     0.263   +11.0 pct   2.412	+ 5.2 pct</p>
<p>   Non-oil mining -  0.036   + 5.1 pct   0.234	+ 3.9 pct</p>
<p> IMPORTS		 9.113   +33.0 pct  50.329	+21.7 pct</p>
<p>Intermediate</p>
<p>	     goods -   7.130   +28.1 pct  39.505	+18.0 pct</p>
<p>   Capital goods -   1.270   +49.4 pct   6.885	+39.3 pct</p>
<p>   Consumer goods -  0.713   +64.0 pct   3.939	+35.3 pct</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9565))</p>
